# NPCs

Each Lua file here is a type of NPC: a person who comes to live in the world. `assets/npc/worldcraft/nurse.lua` is `worldcraft:nurse`. A file returns a table of the fields below, written in Luau (see `assets/item/README.md`: comments, local values, and shared helpers from `assets/lib/`). A key that isn't a plain name is written `["worldcraft:water"] = ...`. There's at most one NPC of each type in a world.

The world's NPC registry, saved with it, decides which NPCs exist:
- **Names:** each type's NPC has one of its personal names, chosen when the world first has the type.
- **Arriving:** an NPC arrives exactly one in-game day after its `arrives` milestone is met, around the player's spawn point (or in a room, once it has one). Without one, it says "<NPC> wants to move in!", and again each day just after sunrise until it has one.
- **Dying:** a dead NPC drops nothing ("<NPC> has died!"), and comes back a day later, beside its table if it has a room, or around the player's spawn point ("<NPC> has recovered!").
- **Shopping:** a merchant's shop is a menu (`assets/menu/worldcraft/shop.lua`, the menus config's `shop`). In it, a Talk button has the merchant say a line, and clicking a ware buys one, onto the stack the cursor holds (refused if that's another item). It's paid from the inventory's coin slots first, then normal slots (the hotbar first, then the smallest stacks), with change from larger coins: back into the coin slots, carrying, or normal slots, or the ground.
- **Talking:** right-clicking an NPC (one in front of a block gets the click) makes it say a line of its `dialogue`.
- **Duplicates:** an NPC's mob that isn't the one the registry names (a copy in an old chunk) is removed when it loads.

| Field | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `role` | What it's called after its name: "Nurse" makes "Jenny the Nurse". Required. |
| `names` | The personal names one may have: one is chosen at random. Required. |
| `mob` | The mob type it's drawn and moves as (`worldcraft:human`, the shared person model), with its numbers. It has none of that mob's spawn rules, drops, coins or attack. Required. |
| `skin` | Its skin, in place of the mob's: `worldcraft:skin_npc_nurse`. |
| `color` | `"#rrggbb"`, or `{r, g, b}` from 0 to 1: the colour of its messages in chat. White by default. |
| `dialogue` | What it says when right-clicked: a list of `{line = "...", when = "any", after = <milestone>}`. One of the lines whose conditions hold now is said at random, in chat as "Jenny the Nurse: <line>", in its colour. `when` is `any` (the default), `day` or `night`; `after` (optional) is a milestone, as `arrives`, that must have been met. Talked to, it stops and faces the player for 5 seconds. |
| `wares` | It's a merchant, selling these: a list of `{item = "worldcraft:bandage", price = 100, after = <milestone>}`, the price in copper (written out by coin in its tooltip: "1 silver"). Wares are unlimited, and can't be sold back. `after` (optional) is a milestone that must have been met first; once it has, the ware stays. Right-clicking a merchant holding a coin opens its shop (holding anything else, it talks). |
| `arrives` | A milestone: it arrives a day after this is first met. `{mined = <block or blocks>, count = n}` or `{used = <item or items>, count = n}`, the count between the things named, 1 by default. Without it (or `starts`), it never arrives by itself. It can be a function instead, met once it returns `true` (below). |
| `starts` | `true`: it's in the world from the start, beside the player when a world first has it (the Librarian), instead of arriving. |
| `talk` | A function run first when it's talked to (below): if it returns `true` it has said what it had to, and its `dialogue` isn't chosen from. The Librarian's first lines, and what she gives, are hers. |

## Functions

An NPC file can have functions, called with a `ctx` as items' and blocks' are (`assets/item/README.md`): tables of functions called with a colon.

- **`talk(ctx)`**, run when it's talked to, before its lines. It returns `true` if it said what it had to.
- **A line's `when`** can be a function: the line can be said while it returns `true`. It's asked when the NPC is talked to.
- **`arrives`, and `after` on a line or a ware,** can be functions: met once they return `true`, and met for good after that. They're asked only when a count changes (a block mined, an item used) and once a day, not every frame, so they can only look at the counts and the days.

```lua
-- Arrives once the player has mined ten coal ore and the world is three days old.
arrives = function(ctx)
  return ctx.milestones:mined("worldcraft:coal_ore") >= 10 and ctx.world:days() >= 3
end,
```

| `ctx` | |
|---|---|
| `ctx.npc:name()`, `:full_name()`, `:role()` | "Jenny", "Jenny the Nurse", "Nurse". In `talk` and `when`. |
| `ctx.npc:has_room()` | Whether it has a room. |
| `ctx.npc:say(text)` | Say something in chat, as "Jenny the Nurse: text", in its colour. |
| `ctx.npc:give(item, n)` | In `talk`: throw `n` of an item (1 if left out) in front of it, towards the player, as the player throws one. |
| `ctx.npc:talk()` | In a menu open on it (its shop): say a line, as when it's talked to. |
| `ctx.npc:get(name)`, `:set(name, n)` | Whole numbers it keeps (what it has said or given), saved with the world; 0 for one never set. |
| `ctx.milestones:used(item)`, `:mined(block)` | In a milestone function: how many the player has used or mined. |
| `ctx.world:days()` | Days the world has run. With `:time_of_day()`, `:is_night()` and `:message(text)`, as for items. |

-- In the world from the start, beside the player when they first spawn:
-- she asks them for a room on the first day, gives a Large Bandage once she
-- has one, and sells what a room needs.

local NIGHTFALL = 0.77
local SUNRISE = 0.23

-- Whether it's still the world's first day: from its start until the first
-- sunrise after its first nightfall.
local function first_day(ctx)
  local days = ctx.world:days()
  -- The time of day the world started at.
  local start = (ctx.world:time_of_day() - days) % 1
  -- Its first nightfall (now, if it started at night), then the sunrise
  -- after it.
  local night = (start >= SUNRISE and start < NIGHTFALL) and (NIGHTFALL - start) or 0
  local dawn = night + (SUNRISE - (start + night)) % 1
  return days < dawn
end

return {
  role = "Librarian",
  names = {"Anais", "Clara", "Cleo", "Talia"},
  mob = "worldcraft:human",
  skin = "worldcraft:skin_npc_librarian",
  color = "#7E5471",
  starts = true,
  wares = {
    {item = "worldcraft:table", price = 100},
    {item = "worldcraft:clipboard", price = 100},
  },
  -- Her first lines, before her ordinary ones: what she's said is kept as
  -- "step" (0: thanks for a room to give; 1: done).
  talk = function(ctx)
    local step = ctx.npc:get("step")
    if step == 0 and ctx.npc:has_room() then
      ctx.npc:say("*Thank you.* Here, have this.")
      ctx.npc:give("worldcraft:large_bandage")
      ctx.npc:set("step", 1)
      return true
    end
    if not ctx.npc:has_room() and first_day(ctx) then
      ctx.npc:say("It will be dark soon. You should make us a shelter. This world is filled with monsters...")
      return true
    end
    return false
  end,
  dialogue = {
    {line = "Have you found diamonds yet?", when = "day"},
    {line = "Have you noticed those shadows in the sky?", when = "day"},
    {line = "I don't imagine you have anything I could read?", when = "day"},
    {line = "Be careful placing torches out in the open. The night winds often blow them out. Or maybe it's the monsters...", when = "night"},
    {line = "Don't stay holed up in here all night. There's still things to be done!", when = "night"},
    {line = "Did you hear that? I don't like it...", when = "night"},
  },
}
return {
