# Isometric screenshots (#276): F11 (here `iso_screenshot`) saves a 2:1
# pixel isometric picture of the square of chunks round the player, 2R
# chunks across for a view distance of R, cropped to the heights of the land
# in it. It waits until every chunk in the square is drawn, so it has no
# gaps. At the default 4 pixels per block and view 4, it's 2048 pixels wide.
# worldcraft --demo demos/iso_screenshot.demo --demo-out demo_out
seed 1
mobs off
view 4
window 1280 720

wait_loaded
time 0.5
iso_screenshot iso-spawn
